Disable VICE's embedded ROM set.

vice-libretro compiles Commodore's KERNAL, BASIC and CHARGEN ROMs into the
core (retrodep/embedded/, gated on USE_EMBEDDED in include/config.h). Those
ROMs are "Copyright C by Commodore Business Machines" per VICE's own README
and carry no redistribution grant -- the GPLv2 covers VICE's code, not them.
A core built with them embedded cannot be redistributed.

VICE supports building without them: retrodep/embedded.h stubs
embedded_check_file() to 0 and embedded_palette_load() to -1 when
USE_EMBEDDED is undefined, so sysfile.c falls through to normal file
loading. The C64 then needs kernal-901227-03.bin, basic-901226-01.bin and
chargen-901225-01.bin supplied at runtime, which is what upstream VICE
proper does.

Verified: rebuilt archive has no CBMBASIC signature, no BASIC banner and no
KERNAL strings; a wasmcart VICE cart with the three ROMs supplied through
its VFS boots and runs a .prg to gameplay.

diff --git a/include/config.h b/include/config.h
index 3fb6692..de10621 100644
--- a/include/config.h
+++ b/include/config.h
@@ -3,7 +3,10 @@
 
 #include <retro_endianness.h>
 
-#define USE_EMBEDDED 1
+/* USE_EMBEDDED disabled: the embedded set is Commodore-copyrighted
+   KERNAL/BASIC/CHARGEN. VICE stubs embedded_check_file() to 0 when this
+   is off (retrodep/embedded.h), so ROMs load from the filesystem. */
+/* #define USE_EMBEDDED 1 */
 
 #if defined(__WIN32__) 
 #define WINDOWS_COMPILE
